Thanks for the explanation! 🍉 

For context, here is our current changeset model, as defined in Akula
```
type Location = H256;
type Value = H256;

// When an account/slot is changed, current block and its old value is written here
decl_table!(AccountChangeSet => BlockNumber => (Address, EncodedAccount);
decl_table!(StorageChangeSet => (BlockNumber, Address, Incarnation) => (Location, Value) => StorageChangeSeekKey);

// Optional history index, used to find account/storage at `earliest block when changed >= requested historical block`
decl_table!(AccountHistory => (Address, BlockNumber) => RoaringTreemap);
decl_table!(StorageHistory => (Address, H256, BlockNumber) => RoaringTreemap);
```

If I read your explanation correctly, you completely replaced current state table, and just use something like changesets directly
